<!-- @before 1. The Metrics That Matter :: guide -->
### Keep denominator and encoding with the value

Play and Crashlytics metrics use different populations and definitions. Align window, version, cohort and freshness before comparing them. Verify the real API’s numeric encoding at the adapter boundary; the source converter deliberately requires an explicit fraction-or-percent contract. [Play crash-rate metric](https://developers.google.com/play/developer/reporting/reference/rest/v1beta1/vitals.crashrate) and [Crashlytics definitions](https://firebase.google.com/docs/crashlytics/crash-free-metrics).

<!-- @before 8. Time Windows And Sample Size :: staff -->
### Separate hold, halt and override

Insufficient evidence supports a hold. A demonstrated regression can require a halt and installed-user mitigation. Any override needs the deciding owner, reason, scope and revisit trigger; it must not silently rewrite missing telemetry as a passing observation.
